WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.671 --> 00:00:03.796
- [Female Speaker] One
core trait in every dog is

00:00:03.796 --> 00:00:05.968
its ever-forgiving nature.

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:08.099
That's probably the most
valuable thing in a dog

00:00:08.099 --> 00:00:10.877
and it's also its biggest pitfall because

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:13.842
we have dogs here who've
been horribly hurt by

00:00:13.842 --> 00:00:16.477
human beings and yet all they want to do

00:00:16.477 --> 00:00:18.163
is find somebody else to love.

00:00:18.163 --> 00:00:20.746
(upbeat music)

00:00:24.789 --> 00:00:26.425
- [Narrator] Around
the world strays, mutts

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:28.841
and street dogs are victims of stigma.

00:00:28.841 --> 00:00:32.182
In Costa Rica, Lya Battle is
trying to change that story.

00:00:32.182 --> 00:00:34.234
She runs the Territorio de Zaguates

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.922
It's a lush haven for
stray dogs to either be

00:00:36.922 --> 00:00:39.837
adopted or live out
the rest of their days.

00:00:39.837 --> 00:00:44.004
- Territorio de Zaguates
stands for land of the mutts.

00:00:45.142 --> 00:00:47.912
My name's Lya Battle, better
known as crazy dog lady,

00:00:47.912 --> 00:00:48.745
I guess.

00:00:48.745 --> 00:00:52.374
I started Territorio de
Zaguates partly because

00:00:52.374 --> 00:00:55.624
I've always loved animals, all animals.

00:00:56.747 --> 00:00:59.769
But it wasn't in my plans,
it wasn't like I set out

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:01.140
to do this.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.854
The need for this, I think
all over the world is

00:01:03.854 --> 00:01:06.539
because there's a huge stigma around a dog

00:01:06.539 --> 00:01:08.820
that doesn't have a breed.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:11.145
They'll let mutts wander on the streets

00:01:11.145 --> 00:01:12.779
or they'll actually
toss them on the streets

00:01:12.779 --> 00:01:15.267
because they're not breed dogs.

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:17.575
The solution isn't euthanizing a dog.

00:01:17.575 --> 00:01:20.992
The solution is make sure it's
not born in the first place.

00:01:20.992 --> 00:01:23.072
Once it's here, do something good for it.

00:01:23.072 --> 00:01:25.472
Find a home or if not at
least offer him a place

00:01:25.472 --> 00:01:28.799
where he can be in peace and happy.

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:30.375
- [Narrator] Keeping
Territorio up and running

00:01:30.375 --> 00:01:31.891
is no easy feat.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:34.980
They eat $500 a day in food alone.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.363
Lya has to work a full time
job to keep all the dogs

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.878
fed and healthy.

00:01:38.878 --> 00:01:42.961
- Territorio stays about
partly through miracles,

00:01:43.849 --> 00:01:44.958
I think.

00:01:44.958 --> 00:01:47.875
Keeping this afloat is a huge task.

00:01:48.757 --> 00:01:51.014
It's a labor of love.

00:01:51.014 --> 00:01:55.181
You can't pay someone to
care for an animal, truly,

00:01:56.117 --> 00:01:59.510
to remember their names,
to be gentle to them.

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:02.021
- [Narrator] While this place
is a dog heaven, nothing

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.100
beats getting adopted by a loving family.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.895
- [Lya] I say it's like
kids at Kindergarten.

00:02:05.895 --> 00:02:08.470
They love their friends at school, but oh,

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.787
they all want to go home to Mom and Dad.

00:02:10.787 --> 00:02:14.954
(upbeat music)
(barking)

